{"v":1,"id":"trial#1","at":"2026-11-05T14:53:55.699Z","kind":"engine.transition","source":{"system":"harness","ref":"return toolu_01Gid1fTbQpKVMhMKFvnU7Xs"},"session":"owner","item":"trial","state":"\"building\"","release":"0.1.0","payload":{"transition":"trial#1","seq":1,"outcome":"applied","reason":null,"workflow":"quick-fix@6a0b9dfd27e783ce29b1cb1e9a911c57862760f7586d2638ce672ae50d9e9d8d","event":{"type":"xstate.done.actor.brief","output":{"builder":"1. Open .github/workflows/test.yml and find the job that runs npm test. Read how it sets up Node today (it uses Node 20 only).\n2. Change that job to use a matrix: `strategy: matrix: node-version: [20, 22]`. Make the actions/setup-node step use `node-version: ${{ matrix.node-version }}`. Keep every other step, including the `npm test` step, running in each matrix leg. Keep the YAML valid and the existing triggers unchanged.\n3. Do not edit tests or source to get green unless a failure is caused by Node 22 itself; if one is, fix its root cause and say so in the PR body.\n4. Run `npm ci` (or the install step the workflow uses) and `npm test` locally and confirm they pass. If Node 22 is available locally (for example via `npx -p node@22 node -v`, nvm or similar), also run `npm test` under it.\n5. Check the workflow file parses as YAML.\n6. Open one pull request containing only this change, with a short description of what changed and why (the invoice service is moving to Node 22).","verifier":"Run every check at the pull request head.\n\nCheck 1: \".github/workflows/test.yml runs npm test on Node 20 and on Node 22 (a matrix over node-version)\"\nRun: parse .github/workflows/test.yml as YAML (for example `ruby -ryaml -e 'p YAML.load_file(\".github/workflows/test.yml\")'` or `python3 -I -c` with yaml, or `node` with a YAML parser if present). Inspect the parsed structure, and also read the CI check results for the head if available.\nPASS: the file parses, a job that runs `npm test` has strategy.matrix.node-version containing both 20 and 22 (any notation, such as 20, \"20\", 20.x), and the job's setup-node step takes its node version from matrix.node-version.\nFAIL: the file does not parse, the matrix is missing, either 20 or 22 is absent, the setup-node step does not use the matrix value, or no step runs `npm test`.\n\nCheck 2: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: `npm ci` (if the repo has a lockfile, else `npm install`) then `npm test` at the head.\nPASS: `npm test` finishes successfully.\nFAIL: `npm test` fails or cannot run.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS or FAIL):\n- If Node 22 is available, also run `npm test` under it and report the result.\n- Check that the PR's CI shows both a Node 20 and a Node 22 leg of the test job, and that both are green.\n- Check that the exact `npm test` exit status is 0, that triggers in the workflow are unchanged, and that the diff touches nothing unrelated.\n- The live Actions run on the matrix can only be fully seen after merge; do not read it as a requirement."}},"run":"trial:0.brief","from":"\"briefing\"","hash":"9b45aab39b05","writes":[{"path":"briefs","from":"event.output","set":"/states/briefing/invoke/onDone/actions/0"}]}}
